Your study of arcane forces has let you develop a new way of applying your aptitude for trapping and poisons.

You gain 1.0 mastery in the {{ct|Cunning}}/{{c|Poisons}} and {{ct|Cunning}}/{{c|Trapping}} talent trees.<br>
Your {{t|Venomous Strike}} talent cooldown is reduced by 3.<br>
Your {{t|Lure}} talent cooldown is reduced by 5.

You learn the following talents:

{{t|Vulnerability Poison}}

Whenever you apply Deadly Poison, you also apply an unresistable magical poison dealing {{cSS|Mag|20|50|0.75}} arcane damage (based on your Magic) each turn. This poison reduces all damage resistance by 10% and poison immunity by 50%.

{{t|Gravitic Trap}}

Lay a trap that creates a radius 5 gravitic anomaly when triggered by foes approaching within range 1.  Each turn, the anomaly deals 10 + 10*(1 + {{cTS|25|100}}/100)*{{cSS|Mag|1|5}} temporal damage (based on your Magic) to foes while pulling them towards its center (chance increases with your combat accuracy or spell power, whichever is higher).<br>
Each anomaly lasts floor({{cTL|10|3|5}}) turns (up to the amount of time since the last anomaly dissipated, based on your Trap Mastery skill).<br>
The trap may trigger more than once, but requires at least 2 turns to recharge between activations.<br>
This design does not require advanced preparation to use.
